// The memory conformance package. Its `test/` directory calls every exported
// name of `core/alloc` and pins the numbers the cost model defines.
//
// The numbers are the point. `design/native/MEMORY.md` §7.1 makes the charge a
// *definition* computed from the types rather than a measurement, so this file
// asserting `16 + n` is not a JavaScript fact — the native suite runs the same
// assertions and gets the same integers, and a backend that disagreed with one
// of them would be wrong rather than merely different.
